{"name":"Petrel","hex":"#4076b4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"petrel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various species of black, grey, or white seabirds in the order Procellariiformes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/petrel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Procellariiformes","blocks":[{"text":"Procellariiformes is an order of seabirds that comprises four families; the albatrosses, the petrels and shearwaters, and two families of storm petrels. Formerly called Tubinares and still called tubenoses in English, Procellariiformes are often referred to collectively as the petrels, a term that has been applied to all members of the order, or more commonly all the families except the albatrosses. They are almost exclusively pelagic, and have a cosmopolitan distribution across the world's oceans, with the highest diversity being the seas around New Zealand."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Thalassarche_bulleri_in_flight_3_-_SE_Tasmania.jpg/330px-Thalassarche_bulleri_in_flight_3_-_SE_Tasmania.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Procellariiformes","wikidata":"Q21685"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Pterodroma_macroptera_Godman.jpg/500px-Pterodroma_macroptera_Godman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Pterodroma_macroptera_Godman.jpg/500px-Pterodroma_macroptera_Godman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pterodroma macroptera from Godman's Monograph of the Petrels, 1907–1910","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APterodroma_macroptera_Godman.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/070226_southern_royal_albatross_off_Kaikoura_2.jpg/500px-070226_southern_royal_albatross_off_Kaikou